<|start|>assistant<|channel|>final<|message|>Below is a **complete, ready‑to‑paste** workflow that

1. gets every member that has ever interacted with a Facebook group page  
2. extracts the profile data for each member  
3. writes those rows into a Google Sheets tab.

Everything is expressed in Sim’s YAML format so you can copy‑and‑paste it directly into your “beflow” canvas (or use the visual editor to tweak as needed).

> **Assumptions**  
> * You already have a Facebook Group ID (`GROUP_ID`) and an access token (`FB_ACCESS_TOKEN`).  
> * You own a Google Sheets spreadsheet identified by its `SHEET_ID` and you have a bearer token for Sheets (`GOOGLE_SHEETS_TOKEN`).  
> * The target tab is named **“Lead‑Profiles”**; the API call will write to range **Sheet1!A:D** (adjust if your sheet uses another name/position).  

---

## 1️⃣ YAML – Full Workflow

```yaml
version: '1.0'
blocks:
  # ───── Starter ────────────────────────────────────────────
  start:
    type: starter
    name: Start
    inputs:
      startWorkflow: schedule
      scheduleType: daily          # run every day
      dailyTime: "09:00"          # UTC time
      timezone: "UTC"
    connections:
      success: fetch-members

  # ───── Fetch group members (Facebook Graph API) ────────
  fetch-members:
    type: api
    name: Get Group Members
    inputs:
      url: "https://graph.facebook.com/v18.0/{{GROUP_ID}}/members?access_token={{FB_ACCESS_TOKEN}}"
      method: GET
      headers:
        - id: h1
          cells: { Key: "Accept", Value: "application/json" }
      timeout: 40000
    connections:
      success: member-loop

  # ───── Loop over each member ID ────────────────────────────
  member-loop:
    type: loop
    name: Member Loop
    inputs:
      loopType: forEach
      collection: <fetchMembers.data.members>   # array of member objects
    connections:
      loop:
        start: fetch-profile-api

  # ───── Fetch profile details for one member (Graph API) ──
  fetch-profile-api:
    type: api
    name: Get Profile
    inputs:
      url: "https://graph.facebook.com/v18.0/<loop.currentItem>?fields=id,name,email,link&access_token={{FB_ACCESS_TOKEN}}"
      method: GET
      headers:
        - id: h1
          cells: { Key: "Accept", Value: "application/json" }
      timeout: 30000
    connections:
      success: format-row

  # ───── Format a single row for Sheets ────────────────────
  format-row:
    type: function
    name: Profile Row
    inputs:
      code: |
        // <loop.currentItem> is the member ID returned by fetch‑members.
        const m = <fetchProfileApi.data>;          // raw Graph response
        return {
          id:   m.id,
          name: m.name,
          email:m.email || "",
          link: m.link  || ""
        };
    connections:
      success: loop.output   # this is the output that will be collected by the loop

  # ───── Build the JSON payload for Sheets API ─────────────
  build-sheet-payload:
    type: function
    name: Sheet Payload
    inputs:
      code: |
        const rows = <memberLoop.results>;
        return {
          majorDimension:"ROWS",
          values: rows.map(r => [r.id, r.name, r.email, r.link])
        };
    connections:
      success: write-sheets

  # ───── Write the rows into Google Sheets ────────────────────
  write-sheets:
    type: api
    name: Write to Sheets
    inputs:
      url: "https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/{{SHEET_ID}}/values?valueInputOption=USER_ENTERED"
      method: PATCH
      headers:
        - id: sh1
          cells: { Key: "Authorization", Value: "Bearer {{GOOGLE_SHEETS_TOKEN}}" }
        - id: sh2
          cells: { Key: "Content-Type", Value: "application/json" }
      body: |
        {
          "range":"Sheet1!A:D",
          "majorDimension":"ROWS",
          "values":<buildSheetPayload.output.values>
        }
      timeout: 60000
    connections:
      success: response

  # ───── Final Response (terminates the workflow) ────────────
  response:
    type: response
    name: End
    inputs:
      Status Code: 200
      Response Data: |
        {
          "status":"Success",
          "rowsWritten": <buildSheetPayload.output.values.length>
        }
```

> **What each block does**  
> *`start`* – triggers the job every morning at 9 am UTC.  
> *`fetch-members`* – calls Facebook Graph to list all current group members.  
> *`member-loop`* – iterates over that member array; for each iteration it runs `fetch-profile-api` and then `format-row`. The loop aggregates the output of `format-row` into `<memberLoop.results>` (array of rows).  
> *`build-sheet-payload`* – turns that array into the exact JSON required by the Sheets API.  
> *`write-sheets`* – pushes the payload to your spreadsheet, writing into columns A‑D of “Sheet1”.  
> *`response`* – emits a 200 status and a short summary.

