## 2️⃣ Environment Variables

| Variable | Purpose | Value Example |
|----------|---------|---------------|
| `GROUP_ID` | ID of the Facebook group you are scraping | `"123456789"` |
| `FB_ACCESS_TOKEN` | OAuth token for Graph API | `"EAAG..."` |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Key for any LLM calls (if you decide to replace one of the functions with an Agent) | `"sk‑xxxxxx"` |
| `SHEET_ID` | ID of the Google Sheets spreadsheet | `"1aBcDEFGHIJKlmnopQrsTuvWX"` |
| `GOOGLE_SHEETS_TOKEN` | Bearer token for Sheets API (you can store it in Sim’s environment section) | `"ya29…"` |

*Tip:* In your workspace, go to **Settings → Environment Variables** and add those four keys. Then the workflow will resolve `<GROUP_ID>`, `<FB_ACCESS_TOKEN>`, etc., automatically.

---

## 3️⃣ Deploying & Testing

1. **Paste** the YAML into a new canvas or copy‑paste it into Sim’s visual editor.  
2. Verify that all connections point to existing blocks – you should see a green “ready” status on every block.  
3. Test manually: click *Run → Manual* and confirm that the final response shows `rowsWritten` ≥ 1 (you’ll see that in the execution log).  
4. Schedule it for production by leaving the starter as is; Sim will run it at 9 am UTC daily.

